+
+---
+
+## 4. Critical checkout/wallet/payment fixes (pre-launch blockers)
+
+A follow-up review surfaced eight issues that made checkout and the wallet
+actively exploitable — not just incomplete. All were verified against the
+code and fixed:
+
+| # | Issue | Fix |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `wallet.topUp` credited the balance instantly with no provider contact — anyone signed in could mint unlimited Kwacha | Top-ups now insert a `pending` transaction only; `wallet.balance` sums **only `completed`** transactions. A new `server/routers/paymentWebhook.ts` is the only code path allowed to mark one `completed`, gated behind a per-provider secret that must be configured in the environment (see file for what's left to wire up with real Airtel/MTN/Zamtel credentials) |
+| 2 | `order.create` took `price`/`subtotal`/`total` straight from the client | Client now sends only `{productId, quantity}` per line item; the server looks up every price from `products` and computes subtotal/shipping/total itself |
+| 3 | Every "payment method" behaved like free checkout — no STK push, no webhook, no way to become "paid" | Mobile-money orders now stay `status: "pending"` until a real webhook confirms them (same webhook file as #1, generalized for order payments is the next step — see follow-ups below); only wallet orders can go straight to `"paid"`, because that's an internal ledger movement of funds already in the platform wallet |
+| 4 | Wallet debit had no balance floor — could go negative | `order.create` now checks completed balance ≥ order total before allowing a WALLET checkout, inside the same transaction |
+| 5 | No stock check or decrement — infinite overselling | Checkout now locks the relevant product rows (`for("update")`), rejects if `stock < quantity`, and decrements stock as part of the same transaction |
+| 6 | Order, order items, wallet debit, and notification were 4 separate inserts — a crash mid-checkout could leave inconsistent state | The entire `order.create` mutation is now one `db.transaction(...)` — all inserts commit together or none do |
+| 7 | "M-Pesa" offered as a payment option — that's Kenyan/Tanzanian, not available in Zambia | Replaced everywhere (wallet, checkout, product detail, schema comments) with **Airtel Money / MTN MoMo / Zamtel Kwacha** |
+| 8 | No delivery address ever collected | `Cart.tsx` now collects address + phone before checkout; `orders` table has `deliveryAddress`, `deliveryPhone`, `deliveryLat`, `deliveryLng` |
+
+Schema changes are in `db/migrations/0004_checkout_payment_fixes.sql`
+(additive/nullable-or-defaulted, safe against existing rows).
+
+### Lower-severity items also fixed
+- `orderItems.productId` now has a real foreign key to `products.id`
+  (migration 0004; added `not valid` so it doesn't fail if any pre-existing
+  rows are orphaned — validate it separately once you've checked for that).
+- The catalog seed file (`0002_expanded_catalog_seed.sql`) had two rows using
+  double-quoted strings, which Postgres parses as identifiers, not string
+  literals — that would have broken the whole insert. Fixed to proper
+  `''`-escaped literals. The products insert is now also idempotent (a
+  `where not exists` guard keyed on name+vendor), matching how the
+  categories insert already worked.
+
+### Still open — flagged, not built this round
+- **Chilimba calculator has no backend.** It's UI-only; no table tracks
+  actual installment schedules or payments against a real order. Worth its
+  own schema (`chilimba_plans`, `chilimba_payments`) and router before it's
+  presented as a real feature to buyers.
+- **No escrow-PIN mechanism exists**, despite being a stated feature
+  somewhere in the product vision. This needs a design decision (what
+  triggers escrow, who holds the PIN, how release works) before it's worth
+  building — flagging rather than guessing at that design.
+- **Mobile money order payments** still just sit at `pending` forever right
+  now, since finishing that requires real Airtel/MTN/Zamtel merchant
+  credentials to actually initiate an STK push and receive the matching
+  webhook. The receiving side (`paymentWebhook.ts`) is scaffolded for wallet
+  top-ups; extending it to confirm order payments too is a small follow-up
+  once those credentials exist.
